# LINE ENDINGS ARE PINNED, ON EVERY PLATFORM.
#
# Not because anything was broken without it. This was added after a wrong
# diagnosis (FK-16): a Linux process inspecting a Windows clone over a file
# bridge reported 56 files modified, because that process never saw the global
# core.autocrlf=true the Windows machine reads. On the machine that owns the
# files, the tree was clean.
#
# Pinning is still right, for one reason worth stating and no others: every
# platform then checks out IDENTICAL BYTES, so a reading taken from one machine
# describes the other. An unpinned repository quietly makes cross-platform
# inspection unreliable, and this kit is inspected across platforms constantly.
#
# The cost, since it is real: a clone that already holds CRLF goes dirty the
# first time these attributes apply, until one `git reset --hard` renormalises
# it. That is a one-time cost of pinning, not the repair of a fault.
#
# This kit is Python, Markdown and JSON. It has no file that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
